    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "〜なら: if so (starting from what was said)",
     "texto": [
      "To answer something already known or just said by the other person: plain-form sentence + **なら**: **にほん へ いく なら、 わたし も いきます** (if you're going to Japan, I'll go too).",
      "It differs from 〜たら: here you start from information already known."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "With nouns and -な adjectives",
     "texto": [
      "**なら** is added directly to the noun or -な adjective: **ひま なら** (if you're free) / **学生 なら** (if you're a student).",
      "**です** isn't added before **なら**; in polite speech forms like **学生でしたら** can be used."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
